s","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T20:12:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T20:12:36Z","body":"Yep.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5444678275/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5449334046","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122246#issuecomment-5449334046","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122246","id":5449334046,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRM49Hg","user":{"login":"distmed","id":265075960,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8y8-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265075960?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed","html_url":"https://github.com/distmed","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T06:42:29Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T06:42:29Z","body":"I have rebased the PR. While testing, I noticed that dragging a built-in script from another scene into the Inspector currently has the same behavior.\r\nI think making the script unique will be the most natural behavior as to restricting the drop. I'm still learning my way around the editor, but should I try to implement that behavior for both `SceneTreeEditor` and the Inspector?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5449334046/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5449608519","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122246#issuecomment-5449608519","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122246","id":5449608519,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRNJtRw","user":{"login":"YeldhamDev","id":30739239,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNzM5MjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30739239?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev","html_url":"https://github.com/YeldhamDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/YeldhamDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T07:16:34Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T07:16:34Z","body":"> should I try to implement that behavior for both `SceneTreeEditor` and the Inspector?\r\n\r\nPreferably, because the problem affects both.\r\n\r\n> I'm still learning my way around the editor,\r\n\r\nFeel free to ask in the [dev chat](https://chat.godotengine.org) if you need help.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5449608519/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5453442832","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122246#issuecomment-5453442832","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122246","id":5453442832,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRQzvEA","user":{"login":"distmed","id":265075960,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8y8-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265075960?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed","html_url":"https://github.com/distmed","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T14:00:55Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T14:00:55Z","body":"I have added checks for built-in scripts from different scenes in both `SceneTreeEditor` and `EditorInspector`.\r\nWhen a script is from another scene, it is duplicated and assigned a new unique ID and path bound to the current scene. When the scene is saved, the path updates while maintaining the unique ID. I haven't found any errors caused by this behavior.\r\nFor the inspector, I check the resource being dropped in `EditorInspector::_edit_set()`. I introduced a `new_value` variable, which stores `p_value` or the duplicated script when needed. I updated the calls that used `p_value` in the method to use `new_value`.\r\nLet me know if this looks like the right approach or if I should handle it differently!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5453442832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5456771855","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122246#issuecomment-5456771855","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122246","id":5456771855,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRT-7Dw","user":{"login":"distmed","id":265075960,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8y8-A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265075960?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed","html_url":"https://github.com/distmed","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/distmed/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-